<title>NORWAY: Storebrand 9-month group result falls.</title>
<headline>Storebrand 9-month group result falls.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30.</p>
<p>				     (millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Life assurance, Storebrand share   463	 vs	    407</p>
<p>Non-life insurance		     840	 vs	  1,064</p>
<p>Storebrand ASA		   minus 165	 vs   minus  219</p>
<p>Operating result		     3,420	 vs	  3,173</p>
<p>Group consolidated result	    922	 vs	  1,283</p>
<p>NOTE - Norway's largest insurance company on October 1 shortened its name to Storebrand ASA, dropping the word &quot;UNI&quot; as part of a campaign to streamline its image. A Reuter poll of seven analysts forecast a nine-month group consolidated result of 1.13 billion crowns. One analyst recommended to buy the share, three said hold and three said sell.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
